    "millsfield:images_texts": [
      "0.5.9\n2\nSHVIL\nJUN 27\n1130 AM\n1930\nTENN\nIN APPRECIATION OF\nPILOT USHER ROUSCH\nC. A.M. 30\nJUNE 22ND - 23TH\nINTERSTATE ARLINES, INC,\nCHICA00 - - ATLANTA\nNanch Week\n5\n10\nVIA\nAIR\nMAIL\n2107 N. \u003e8ths\nADOLF ALTENBERND,\nBOX T28 ROUTE 2\nBROOKLYN STATION=\nCleveland, Ohio.",
      "1999.023.002 a)",
      "USHER ROUSCH, night mail pilot for Interstate\nAirlines, Inc., on the Atlanta-Evansville section,\nconnecting at Evansville with the Chicago and St.\nLouis lines operated by Interstate. Before join-\ning Interstate Airlines, Rousch did considerable\nflying on the West coast for motion picture compa-\nnies. In one of the pictures his plane was blown\nto pieces by a premature charge of dynamite which\nhad been set for a scene in which an explosion was\nto take place on the ground as the ship flew over.\nPractically every bone was broken, but he recovered."
    ],
